"""The calls the {{title}} connector makes, each answer checked before it is used.

TODO(connector): this is the one module that knows the service's JSON. Take what it needs from the
browser's network tab (docs/connector-guide.md in the catalog-sync repository shows how):

* ``GET /api/v1/items``: one page of the list.
* ``GET /api/v1/items/{id}``: one item's detail record.

The answers are read as ``{"state": true, "data": ...}``, the detail wrapped twice (``data.data``),
because that is a common shape and what tests/fake_service.py serves. A service that does not wrap
its answers: read the block directly and drop ``require_state_ok`` and ``peel_data``. HTTP 200 does
not mean success on every service, so check whatever the service uses to say it failed.
"""

